</code></pre> <p>The code adds the embedded account metadata transaction to an 6251a85a-47d0-11ee-be56-0242ac120002:e28c177ca172b7e7b8b08d9539c0c72d:&lt;__None__&gt;.</p> <p>Since the signer is modifying their own account, no 6251a85a-47d0-11ee-be56-0242ac120002:4c0fc4018df638d90f8c273471a52d3e:&lt;__None__&gt; are required and the aggregate can be created as 6251a85a-47d0-11ee-be56-0242ac120002:946660397d53238783661bf06bf3cc24:, allowing it to be signed and announced immediately. <p>Adding metadata to a different account</p> <p>If the target account is different from the signer, the target must cosign the aggregate transaction to approve the metadata entry.</p> <p>For details on collecting cosignatures on-chain, see the Bonded Aggregate tutorial.</p>

